            <history xml:id="history_250N2017D">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_94e33ae3">
                  <event xml:id="event_d1e609599">
                     <persName role="" xml:id="persName_5174afbb">J.P.E. Hartmann, organ</persName>
                     <date isodate="1826-12-20" xml:id="date_16a7607a">1826-12-20</date>
                     <geogName role="venue" xml:id="geogName_250N2021D">Garnisons Kirke</geogName>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_250N20221">Copenhagen</geogName>
                  </event>
                  <event xml:id="event_286ccc01">
                     <date isodate="1835-10-25" xml:id="date_d2f0992f">1835-10-25</date>
                     <geogName role="venue" xml:id="geogName_293c2f58">Christiansborg Slotskirke</geogName>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_7577b9ca">Copenhagen</geogName>
                     <persName role="" xml:id="persName_cf774f01">J.P.E. Hartmann, organ</persName>
                     <desc xml:id="idm103">In the advertisement the performance is called "Fri Fantasie", so it might not be the published Fantasia.</desc>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_8f3ad402">
                        <head xml:id="head_0a7d8b70">Reviews</head>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_384b4015">
                        <head xml:id="head_c54cec63">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm108">The Fantasia for organ was written for a concert in Garnisons Kirke where Hartmann had been appointed organist two years earlier. The organ was in a very bad state, hence the purpose was to collect money for the repair. The Concert overture, opus 3 (HartW 30) had its first performance at the same concert.</p>
            </history>
